# Using azldev

azldev builds a Linux distribution from TOML configuration. It imports RPM specs
from an upstream distro and customizes them with an overlay system — no spec
forking. Components render to specs and sidecar build inputs, then build into RPMs;
images assemble RPMs into bootable artifacts.

## Orient yourself

- Run azldev from the repo root (where `azldev.toml` lives), or pass `-C <dir>`.
- Global, agent-friendly flags: **`-q`** (quiet) and **`-O json`** (machine-readable
  output). They work on every command.
- Config is a stitched TOML hierarchy: `azldev.toml` includes the distro and project
  config, which include the component files (`**/*.comp.toml`) into one namespace.

## Core concepts

- **Component** — a unit of packaging that renders to a spec and sidecar build inputs,
  then builds into one or more RPMs. Its spec source is upstream (default), a pinned
  upstream distro/version, or a local spec.
- **Overlay** — a semantic patch applied to a spec or source file at render time, so
  you customize upstream without forking it.
- **Distro** — a named build target (`*.distro.toml`) with upstream URIs, release
  versions, and build inputs.
- **Rendered spec** — the generated `.spec` after overlays; a build input, never
  hand-edited.
- **Lock** — a per-component file pinning the resolved upstream commit and an input
  fingerprint.

## Common commands

`lockless-components.txt` beside the top-level `azldev.toml` selects the lockless
workflow per component for all commands. Listed components ignore locks and use
generated upstream-commit TOML instead. All others use locks.
`azldev comp make-lockless` adds selected exact names to that list if needed,
then runs the refresh pipeline. Existing list contents and lock files are retained.
Already-listed components are still refreshed; a refresh failure leaves the list updated.

Before preparing any selected lockless upstream component, rendering requires a
clean project Git repository: staged changes, unstaged tracked changes, and
untracked files anywhere in the repository block the whole invocation.
Git-ignored files are excluded. Use `--allow-uncommitted` for intentional dirty
renders; `--check-only` and `--no-git-commit` do not bypass this check.
The override does not change committed-history carryover or failure recovery.
Locked and local components do not trigger this check.

For listed upstream components, rendering prepares the changelog before Release,
then writes macros, applies overlays, and updates `sources`.
Version detection and carryover use the upstream spec before overlays.
Overlays can override the prepared release and changelog.
Non-autorelease rendering then runs host `rpmdev-bumpspec`, without synthetic history or its legacy
release adjustment. Lockless rendering
preserves the existing spaces and tabs after `Release:` when editing its value, and
compares output before the final release bump; `--check-only` stops before that bump.
Unchanged lockless upstream renders require `--no-change-rebuild`; otherwise rendering errors
without replacing existing output. The flag records host `date -Is` output in
`.no-change-rebuild` before bumping, only when no changes were detected. Comparison
ignores this root marker in both existing output and the working upstream checkout.
Lockless failures never write `RENDER_FAILED`. Before replacement, output is
untouched; failures after replacement starts clear the component directory and
use Git to restore committed output, or leave no directory if none existed.
Recovery discards uncommitted changes in that directory and keeps no backups.
It never uses mock or `rpmautospec process-distgit`; RPM macros remain unexpanded.
It retains all prepared dist-git files except `.git`, without file filtering or
`spectool` queries, and replaces and
automatically commits that component's output directory. The first commit also includes
all staged changes, unstaged tracked changes, and non-ignored untracked files outside
the rendered output directory. Other rendered paths are excluded even if staged;
later commits include only their component's dist-git changes.
`--changelog-comment` supplies the exact `rpmdev-bumpspec -c`
value and commit message, with no default. If omitted, `$EDITOR` or a local editor
collects the entry using a template with two blank lines and `#`-commented instructions.
Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are removed, with no trailing newline;
the cleaned text is reused for the Git message. Explicit flag values remain unchanged.
Autorelease skips `rpmdev-bumpspec`; without a supplied comment, Git prompts
in its own editor for a message, with upstream changes in the template.
Provide `--changelog-comment` for unattended rendering.
`--no-git-commit` skips automatic staging and committing, but still renders and
bumps non-autorelease specs.
Upstream changes remain in the Git commit body, not the changelog comment.
Commit refreshed TOML before rendering. Configure Git author
identity and install `rpmdevtools`. `--check-only` never creates project commits.
Local components skip upstream carryover and automatic commits; locked
components retain their existing render behavior.

Top-level commands in this build:

{{ range .TopLevelCommands }}- `azldev {{ .Name }}` — {{ .Short }}
{{ end }}
Everyday tasks (add `-q -O json` when scripting):

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List components | `azldev comp list -a` |
| Inspect one component | `azldev comp list -p <name>` |
| Add a component | `azldev comp add` |
| Build a component | `azldev comp build -p <name>` |
| Render specs | `azldev comp render -p <name>` (or `-a`) |
| Refresh a lock | `azldev comp update -p <name>` |
| Refresh a lockless component | `azldev comp refresh-upstream-commit -p <name>` |
| List / build images | `azldev image list` / `azldev image build` |

`comp` is an alias for `component`. Always confirm current syntax with
`azldev <command> --help`.

The hidden `advanced` group (`adv`) contains specialist integrations such as MCP and
mock helpers; it is intentionally omitted from normal help.

